# 000-EFF-0019 — The agent names a failed request's method by `Method::name()` — done

**Type:** service · **Owner:** `EFF` · **Priority:** P2 · **Status:** done (2026-10-29) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** — (for `NET`'s [000-NET-0047](../issues/000-NET-0047-http-for-api-clients.md)) · **Constitution:** MC-12.4

## Problem

`NET`'s request (`issues/requests-EFF.md`, 2026-10-28):
- `effector/src/main.rs` named a failed request's method with a `match` over every case of `mind::http::Method`.
- 000-NET-0047 adds `Head`, `Patch` and `Delete`, and a new case would break that `match` outside `libmind`.

## Plan

Name the method with `method.name()`, which `libmind` already makes public.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The agent builds with `method.name()` and names the method as before (`effector`, x86, 2026-10-29).

## Resolution

Done on 2026-10-29 by the `EFF` track.
- **The change:** the log line of a failed request in `effector/src/main.rs` calls `method.name()`. It prints the same words: `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`.
- **The request** is taken out of `issues/requests-EFF.md`.
- **What it frees:** `NET` may add the new cases in 000-NET-0047.
